Answer DNS that the app cannot tie to an owner with addresses only.

With "only selected apps" in keqdroid's VPN the system's own DNS arrives in
the tun with no owner the VPN may see (OEM firmware sending app queries as
AID_DNS, the network stack resolving the Private DNS server name). The app
recognizes it by address, our DNS in the tun, and answers empty so the guard
lets it through (mihomo-uid-owner-guard.patch). An app outside the VPN can
send its own query to the same address, and the hijack relayed it upstream
through the server: "whoami.cloudflare TXT CH" came back with the server
address (checked on a Pixel 6a on 2026-10-22).

Such queries now get A and AAAA answered and everything else refused, the
way xray's dns outbound treats all of them. Queries with a known owner are
untouched. The flag rides the context into resolver.relayDnsPacket, which
all three hijack paths (TCP and both UDP ones) go through.

Applies after mihomo-uid-owner-handshake.patch; the name keeps it sorted
after it.

